    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) leading the charge as the premier start. His matchup against Randy Dobnak (5.16 xERA) is perfectly aligned, bolstered by a 14% boost from dynamic platoon splits and a 10% premium for his spot atop the order. The favorable wind conditions further amplify his potential for stolen bases, our most critical category. Joining him in the elite tier are **Trea Turner** (77.93) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.21), both of whom benefit significantly from facing Shane Bieber\u2019s 5.23 xERA. Despite the high-leverage matchup, the expectation for high volume on base provides a strong floor for these anchors, particularly with **Trea Turner** leveraging his speed profile to capitalize on the weak opposing starter.\n\nStrategic considerations for the remaining slots focused heavily on platoon advantages and tactical park adjustments. **Junior Caminero** (62.17) remains a high-floor play despite the tough park factor, as his strong xwOBA (0.378) and order placement offer reliable offensive output. Meanwhile, **Nelson Velazquez** (59.79) earns the utility start over the bench options, as the combination of his power profile and wind-aided park conditions offsets the moderate efficiency of Michael Lorenzen. **Chase Meidroth** (49.54) serves as our closest non-starter; he was ultimately excluded due to the stiff competition in our middle infield and a projected lower-order batting position that limited his run-production ceiling compared to the primary lineup.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, which introduces non-trivial volatility to our efficiency scores. **Dillon Dingler** (40.00) is currently operating near his floor due to the defensive and platoon-heavy nature of his role against Logan Webb; if the official lineup drops him lower than the projected #3 hole, he is a primary candidate for a mid-day pivot to preserve game caps. Furthermore, while **Christian Yelich** (46.02) carries a respectable projection, his heavy negative platoon split against a lefty like Connor Prielipp keeps him in the marginal category. The Zebras\u2019 success today rests on the top-of-order speedsters, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Trea Turner**, turning those favorable pitching matchups into the high-efficiency baserunning sequences we desperately need to climb the standings.",
